anyOf.description:
How closed contours determine the filled interior.

Recording retains both rules without silently substituting one for
the default NonZero rule.

```
use motion_core::prelude::*;
use motion_core::{
    DisplayList, RasterLimits, ResourceStore, ValidatedDisplayList, MAX_PATH_VERBS,
    MAX_STROKE_VERBS, MAX_SVG_PATH_BYTES, sample_offsets,
};
let path = Path2D::from_rect(Rect::new(0.0, 0.0, 10.0, 20.0))?;
let fill = path.fill(Color::WHITE);
let native = DrawContext::default().record(&fill, ValidationLimits::default())?;
assert!(matches!(
    native[0],
    DrawCommand::Fill {
        rule: FillRule::NonZero,
        ..
    }
));
let even = DrawContext::default().record(
    &fill.fill_rule(FillRule::EvenOdd),
    ValidationLimits::default(),
)?;
assert!(matches!(
    even[0],
    DrawCommand::Fill {
        rule: FillRule::EvenOdd,
        ..
    }
));
# Ok::<(), motion_core::ValidationError>(())
```

description:
A complete declarative film: canvas, frame rate, tracks, audio and look.

Times are seconds, angles are degrees and colors are CSS-style strings.
[`Document::from_json`] and [`Document::to_json`] round-trip the data model;
[`Document::compile`](crate::Document::compile) produces an engine timeline.

```
use motion_scene::{Document, Element, SceneSpec, TrackSpec};
use motion_core::Color;
let document = Document::new([320.0, 180.0], 30).track(TrackSpec::new().scene(
    SceneSpec::new(2.0, Element::circle([160.0, 90.0], 40.0).fill(Color::WHITE)),
));
let json = document.to_json()?;
assert_eq!(Document::from_json(&json)?, document);
# Ok::<(), motion_core::Error>(())
```
